  "id": "COMPOUND:29828 - PROTEIN:6336",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a relationship between the compound 6-[(2E)-3,7-Dimethylocta-2,6-Dienyl]-5,7-Dihydroxy-8-(3-Methylbutanoyl)-4-Phenylchromen-2-One and Thrombopoietin, as it is identified as a target of multiple entities that ultimately lead to Thrombopoietin. SNU-387, a cell line, is targeted by this compound and by other compounds such as Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside, both of which are themselves targets of Thrombopoietin. This indicates that the compound may exert its effects through a mechanism that indirectly influences Thrombopoietin, possibly by modulating cellular pathways or signaling cascades that are involved in thrombopoiesis. The evidence suggests a potential role in the regulation of thrombopoietin, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
